 * Error: Initial charge and total charge of the system are inconsistent.
 *
 * We stop here by default to make users aware and (hopefully) enable better results.
 *
 * Selected charge in control.in:     0.0000
 * Sum of initial charges in geometry.in:     0.0000
 *
 * Background: FHI-aims can run with an initial charge sum that differs from the target
 * charge. However, choosing a different charge than the intended one can lead to rather
 * long or even non-convergent self-consistency cycles, because the starting point is
 * too far away from the intended final ground state density.
 *
 * In some cases, there may even be several different self-consistent solutions for the same
 * geometry and initializing too far away from the intended result may lead to a non-ground
 * state solution being obtained.
 *
 * It is therefore better to initialize with a charge that is close to the intended
 * final result.
 *
 * If you do wish to proceed with a different initial charge sum, this is possible.
 * In that case, please add the keyword
 *
 * override_initial_charge_check .true.
 *
 * to your control.in file. In general, we recommend setting the correct initial charge
 * if that is possible.
 *
